# Task 4 re-review — quantity-path reconciliation fix

## Finding Verdict

**Resolved.** `_validate_episode_quantity_path` replays each filtered `EpisodeId` fill
in its DataFrame order and requires exact path/fill cardinality
(`core/pit_optimizer_v5/diagnostics.py:397-405`). It rejects non-causal session order
and duplicate transitions (`406-423`), maps BUYs to `entry`/`add_on` and SELLs to
`scale_out`/terminal `exit` while accumulating signed position quantity (`425-438`),
and checks each transition's action, session, reason, execution price, and post-fill
quantity (`440-453`). It also reconciles add-on count, first/last fill action,
entry/exit sessions, symbols, execution prices, exit reason, and zero terminal
quantity (`455-480`). The pre-existing fill friction replay validates the action-derived
cash deltas before this function runs (`210-295`).

## New Breakage

None found in the requested fix-only scope. Same-session fills remain supported in their
recorded causal order (`408-410`), while a sell before its corresponding open quantity
fails (`432-436`). Zero-activity still exits through the explicit no-fill branch and
requires no episodes plus unchanged terminal cash (`313-320`).

